    example: "Buy for [[$1,000M]] with [[$600M]] of debt at [[7%]], ignoring taxes and fees. Sell after one year for [[$1,100M]]: repay $642M, leaving $458M on $400M, a 14.5% return against 10.0% unlevered. Sell for [[$950M]] instead: $308M is left, −23.0% against −5.0%. The formula agrees: 10% + (10% − 7%) × 1.5 = 14.5%.",
