    classic: true,
    q: "What makes a company a good LBO candidate?",
    a: "Steady, predictable cash flow that can carry a lot of debt. That usually means recurring revenue, a strong market position and stable margins, plus low capex and working capital needs so EBITDA turns into cash. Add a reasonable price, little existing debt, capable management, clear ways to grow EBITDA and a realistic exit.",
