    q: "How are transaction fees and financing fees treated in an LBO?",
    a: "Both are uses of funds, so both add to the equity check. Transaction fees, paid to advisers, lawyers and accountants for the acquisition, are expensed at closing, reducing equity on the pro forma balance sheet. Financing fees for arranging the debt are capitalized as a reduction of the debt and amortized over its life as non-cash interest expense.",
